WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.435 --> 00:00:01.600
JACK: Have you ever tried installing

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.534
an app on your computer but then

00:00:03.537 --> 00:00:04.615
ended up with something else?

00:00:04.616 --> 00:00:06.139
Like, you downloaded something you

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:08.207
actually wanted like a app to retrieve

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:10.285
a deleted file or to get some video

00:00:10.286 --> 00:00:11.666
to play properly, [Music] you get it

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:13.151
on your machine the way everyone does,

00:00:13.151 --> 00:00:14.662
you downloaded it, run the installer,

00:00:14.665 --> 00:00:16.257
click through the screens, next, next,

00:00:16.258 --> 00:00:18.779
next, agree, and then it’s installed,

00:00:18.779 --> 00:00:20.986
but then something strange happens.

00:00:21.142 --> 00:00:22.457
You might not notice right away, but

00:00:22.457 --> 00:00:24.601
there’s something new on your computer,

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.255
a new app or toolbar in your browser,

00:00:27.256 --> 00:00:28.974
or maybe your homepage changed to

00:00:28.974 --> 00:00:30.647
something like a search engine you

00:00:30.649 --> 00:00:32.522
never heard of, and your computer

00:00:32.522 --> 00:00:33.779
seems to be doing something every now

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.947
and then that just doesn't make sense.

00:00:36.508 --> 00:00:38.549
Like, it’s a tad slower or the

00:00:38.549 --> 00:00:40.722
fans are suddenly louder, but

00:00:40.723 --> 00:00:42.238
you're just not exactly sure why.

00:00:42.705 --> 00:00:44.483
Most of the time it’s relatively harmless.

00:00:44.494 --> 00:00:45.921
It’s some kind of junkware.

00:00:46.229 --> 00:00:48.190
Some company paid a few cents to bundle

00:00:48.193 --> 00:00:49.989
their stuff into your download, hoping

00:00:49.989 --> 00:00:51.357
that you wouldn't remove the software

00:00:51.357 --> 00:00:53.232
and you would start using their software.

00:00:53.394 --> 00:00:54.513
It’s annoying but it’s easy

00:00:54.513 --> 00:00:55.783
to delete and forget about it.

00:00:56.244 --> 00:00:57.715
But stop and think what just happened;

00:00:57.741 --> 00:01:00.068
you went to try to install one thing

00:01:00.313 --> 00:01:01.804
and something else came along with

00:01:01.804 --> 00:01:03.042
it, something you didn't choose to

00:01:03.042 --> 00:01:04.354
download and didn't even know you

00:01:04.354 --> 00:01:05.672
were installing it at the time.

00:01:06.128 --> 00:01:07.610
You didn't even know what it was.

00:01:07.727 --> 00:01:09.257
It latched onto something else

00:01:09.259 --> 00:01:10.981
that you trusted and came into

00:01:10.981 --> 00:01:12.445
your PC and got installed.

00:01:13.003 --> 00:01:14.618
I hate this kind of software,

00:01:14.621 --> 00:01:16.195
software that you didn't install.

00:01:16.196 --> 00:01:18.228
It just came along for the ride, software

00:01:18.231 --> 00:01:19.611
that you don't want on your machine.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.745
It has a hidden agenda, and who

00:01:21.746 --> 00:01:23.188
knows what that thing is doing there.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:26.175
This is a story about a piece of software

00:01:26.175 --> 00:01:28.342
that snuck onto our machines like that.

00:01:28.892 --> 00:01:30.772
It’s called Blackshades.

00:01:34.993 --> 00:01:35.645
Intro: [Intro music] These

00:01:35.645 --> 00:01:36.791
are true stories from the

00:01:36.792 --> 00:01:38.251
dark side of the internet.

00:01:42.086 --> 00:01:43.328
I’m Jack Rhysider.

00:01:44.665 --> 00:01:45.575
This is Darknet Diaries.

00:01:45.575 --> 00:01:45.983
JACK: Let me start at

00:02:03.182 --> 00:02:03.603
beginning.

00:02:03.829 --> 00:02:06.235
Alex Yucel and Michael Hogue created

00:02:06.235 --> 00:02:08.210
a program called Blackshades, and in

00:02:08.211 --> 00:02:10.484
2010 they started selling it online.

00:02:11.019 --> 00:02:12.225
Blackshades, or more

00:02:12.226 --> 00:02:12.396
specifically, the Blackshades RAT,

00:02:14.505 --> 00:02:15.990
is a piece of software that allows

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:17.903
an attacker to gain complete control

00:02:17.915 --> 00:02:19.877
remotely of a victim’s machine.

00:02:20.063 --> 00:02:21.926
They can view their files, record

00:02:21.926 --> 00:02:22.953
their keystrokes, lock their

00:02:22.953 --> 00:02:24.432
data, and hijack their webcam.

00:02:24.445 --> 00:02:25.923
[Music] They marketed Blackshades

00:02:25.937 --> 00:02:27.380
like a regular software product.

00:02:27.384 --> 00:02:29.004
They had a website with an About

00:02:29.004 --> 00:02:30.713
Us page and an Order Now button.

00:02:31.144 --> 00:02:33.424
The page said ‘Blackshades is

00:02:33.425 --> 00:02:35.184
mainly an IT surveillance and

00:02:35.184 --> 00:02:37.431
security-based company directed at

00:02:37.431 --> 00:02:39.787
making your PC experiences easier.

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:42.304
Our main goal is to offer affordable

00:02:42.304 --> 00:02:44.350
software solutions comparable to bigger

00:02:44.352 --> 00:02:46.818
names out there.’ Then they listed

00:02:46.818 --> 00:02:48.414
the benefits of using the product;

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:52.016
to spy on your children or spouse, to

00:02:52.016 --> 00:02:53.641
find out if your partner is cheating

00:02:53.641 --> 00:02:55.611
on you, or to see if someone was

00:02:55.611 --> 00:02:58.170
using your computer in unwanted ways.

00:02:58.796 --> 00:03:00.585
They even had a legal notice saying

00:03:00.899 --> 00:03:02.899
that it’s legal to install monitoring

00:03:02.899 --> 00:03:04.464
software on your own computer

00:03:04.698 --> 00:03:06.822
according to the Spy Act of 2004.

00:03:07.483 --> 00:03:08.058
The price?

00:03:08.366 --> 00:03:09.117
Forty bucks.

00:03:09.939 --> 00:03:12.130
The site wasn't hidden on the dark web.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:13.293
It was right there in the open with

00:03:13.311 --> 00:03:15.271
normal-sounding marketing language, and

00:03:15.271 --> 00:03:17.653
at first glance it doesn't look nefarious.

00:03:17.935 --> 00:03:19.857
But as you think about it, you're

00:03:19.858 --> 00:03:21.148
like, wait, hold on a minute.

00:03:21.628 --> 00:03:24.267
The software is used to spy on people?

00:03:25.373 --> 00:03:26.247
Which makes me wonder,

00:03:26.756 --> 00:03:28.995
is Blackshades legal?

00:03:29.787 --> 00:03:31.210
Well, there’s actually two questions here.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:32.999
Is making and selling Blackshades

00:03:33.011 --> 00:03:35.724
legal, and is using Blackshades legal?

00:03:36.245 --> 00:03:37.590
The website says that this is a

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.065
surveillance and security tool

00:03:39.303 --> 00:03:40.822
used to monitor the activity

00:03:40.846 --> 00:03:41.956
of your child’s computer.

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:44.348
Well, that in itself isn't illegal

00:03:44.348 --> 00:03:46.260
even if it can be abused, kinda

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:47.519
like a knife isn't illegal.

00:03:47.519 --> 00:03:48.686
We need it to make food with.

00:03:49.296 --> 00:03:50.772
Someone waving it around on the

00:03:50.773 --> 00:03:52.377
street is suddenly a big threat.

00:03:53.088 --> 00:03:54.664
In fact, many businesses today use

00:03:54.664 --> 00:03:56.329
software just like that to monitor

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:57.377
what their employees are doing.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:59.069
It’ll take screenshots, record what

00:03:59.085 --> 00:04:00.951
apps are opened and in focus, and

00:04:00.951 --> 00:04:02.516
track the locations of devices.

00:04:03.274 --> 00:04:04.974
But when a company spies on its own

00:04:04.975 --> 00:04:06.793
computers, it typically makes it very

00:04:06.797 --> 00:04:09.167
clear; there is a monitoring system

00:04:09.183 --> 00:04:11.263
on your computer, or they make the

00:04:11.266 --> 00:04:12.873
employees sign a document which says

00:04:12.873 --> 00:04:14.442
‘You may be monitored while you're here

00:04:14.442 --> 00:04:16.728
at work’, which is what makes it legal.

00:04:16.752 --> 00:04:18.043
That person being spied on

00:04:18.055 --> 00:04:19.873
knows and consents to it.

00:04:20.468 --> 00:04:23.222
So, on the surface, both making and using

00:04:23.222 --> 00:04:26.379
software like this can be perfectly legal.

00:04:27.272 --> 00:04:28.638
But Blackshades wasn't

00:04:28.659 --> 00:04:30.695
marketing this to businesses.

00:04:31.253 --> 00:04:33.808
They were marketing it on hacker forums.

00:04:35.487 --> 00:04:36.451
[Music] They specifically were

00:04:36.455 --> 00:04:38.101
building a tool that they knew people

00:04:38.102 --> 00:04:40.491
would use for malicious purposes.

00:04:40.756 --> 00:04:41.830
They weren't in the business

00:04:41.831 --> 00:04:43.455
of selling kitchen knives.

00:04:43.805 --> 00:04:45.303
They were specifically marketing

00:04:45.305 --> 00:04:46.223
their product to people

00:04:46.225 --> 00:04:48.136
they knew would abuse it.

00:04:48.519 --> 00:04:49.686
So, their whole website, which was

00:04:49.687 --> 00:04:51.123
saying this is used to track your kids,

00:04:51.211 --> 00:04:53.363
that was really a lie, a ruse to make

00:04:53.364 --> 00:04:55.867
it look legal and look perfectly fine.

00:04:56.439 --> 00:04:58.133
To the courts, who look at things through

00:04:58.133 --> 00:05:01.654
the lens of the law, intent matters a lot.

00:05:02.181 --> 00:05:03.976
If you know you're selling to people

00:05:03.979 --> 00:05:05.967
who will use it to commit crimes with,

00:05:06.604 --> 00:05:08.364
then yeah, it’s illegal to sell that.

00:05:09.096 --> 00:05:11.513
When it comes to the customers, if

00:05:11.513 --> 00:05:12.537
they were putting it on people’s

00:05:12.544 --> 00:05:14.234
computers without their consent

00:05:14.244 --> 00:05:15.729
and spying on someone without them

00:05:15.729 --> 00:05:17.818
knowing, then that’s illegal, too.

00:05:18.421 --> 00:05:19.921
That’s unauthorized access to

00:05:19.924 --> 00:05:21.561
a computer, privacy violations,

00:05:21.572 --> 00:05:22.813
identity theft, intercepting

00:05:22.815 --> 00:05:24.316
communications, and extortion.

00:05:24.839 --> 00:05:26.392
So yeah, this can be illegal

00:05:26.393 --> 00:05:28.411
to use as well, both illegal

00:05:28.412 --> 00:05:30.022
to make and illegal to use.

00:05:30.479 --> 00:05:31.907
But again, it all comes down

00:05:31.909 --> 00:05:34.030
to intent of whether or not

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:35.914
this is legal versus illegal.

00:05:36.491 --> 00:05:38.503
If these people who use it and make

00:05:38.503 --> 00:05:40.303
it are going to get in trouble over

00:05:40.304 --> 00:05:41.809
this, then the courts are gonna have

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:43.798
to prove that intent was there to

00:05:43.812 --> 00:05:45.838
sell it to criminals or to spy on

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:46.931
people without their permission.

00:05:47.751 --> 00:05:49.633
Blackshades is better known as

00:05:49.633 --> 00:05:52.119
the Blackshades RAT, and RAT

00:05:52.242 --> 00:05:54.565
stands for Remote Access Trojan.

00:05:54.991 --> 00:05:56.389
Remote access is like when you

00:05:56.396 --> 00:05:58.889
need computer help and IT support

00:05:58.907 --> 00:06:00.300
takes over your computer to fix

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:01.918
something, or when you log into your

00:06:01.923 --> 00:06:03.385
home computer from a coffee shop.

00:06:04.018 --> 00:06:05.435
A RAT is the exact same thing,

00:06:05.563 --> 00:06:07.730
except it’s malicious in nature.

00:06:08.138 --> 00:06:10.207
Someone you don't know takes

00:06:10.207 --> 00:06:12.173
over your computer without your

00:06:12.173 --> 00:06:13.634
knowledge or consent, and they

00:06:13.634 --> 00:06:15.298
can see everything you're doing.

00:06:15.828 --> 00:06:17.644
The scariest bit is you have no

00:06:17.644 --> 00:06:19.309
idea it’s happening, since it’s

00:06:19.323 --> 00:06:21.037
completely running silently.

00:06:22.669 --> 00:06:23.895
Once Blackshades was on your

00:06:23.896 --> 00:06:25.381
machine, the attacker has an

00:06:25.382 --> 00:06:27.151
astonishing level of access.

00:06:27.394 --> 00:06:28.729
They could read every file and view

00:06:28.731 --> 00:06:30.626
every photo and video on your computer.

00:06:30.901 --> 00:06:31.512
They could see every

00:06:31.513 --> 00:06:32.620
single key you pressed.

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:34.046
Every password, every credit card

00:06:34.048 --> 00:06:35.289
number, every private message

00:06:35.292 --> 00:06:36.645
went straight to the attacker.

00:06:36.995 --> 00:06:38.807
They could steal the log-ins to your bank,

00:06:38.846 --> 00:06:40.741
your e-mail, your social media accounts.

00:06:41.131 --> 00:06:42.469
They could turn your webcam and

00:06:42.469 --> 00:06:44.265
microphone on, and from there they

00:06:44.267 --> 00:06:46.314
can commit a litany of crimes; theft,

00:06:46.325 --> 00:06:48.922
extortion, blackmail, for example, but

00:06:48.923 --> 00:06:50.855
also wire fraud and identity theft.

00:06:51.373 --> 00:06:52.150
And it gets worse.

00:06:52.386 --> 00:06:53.659
Blackshades had a feature

00:06:53.699 --> 00:06:55.048
called the Spreader.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:56.699
Once it was on your computer, the

00:06:56.701 --> 00:06:58.743
attacker could use your social media

00:06:58.743 --> 00:07:00.607
accounts and chat apps to try to spread

00:07:00.608 --> 00:07:02.178
it to your friends’ computers, too.

00:07:02.749 --> 00:07:03.994
They could even use Blackshades

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:06.286
for ransomware, locking up their

00:07:06.286 --> 00:07:07.895
targets’ files and demanding

00:07:07.895 --> 00:07:09.427
payments to unscramble them.

00:07:09.427 --> 00:07:11.971
[Music] I can't imagine this feature

00:07:12.036 --> 00:07:14.356
being used for any legitimate purpose.

00:07:14.804 --> 00:07:16.686
So, the fact that this had a ransomware

00:07:16.695 --> 00:07:18.335
feature squarely puts it in the

00:07:18.335 --> 00:07:20.013
malicious software territory, if you're

00:07:20.013 --> 00:07:22.539
asking me, making it clearly illegal.

00:07:23.094 --> 00:07:24.996
But Blackshades would make their users

00:07:24.998 --> 00:07:26.630
click on a button stating that the

00:07:26.631 --> 00:07:28.856
user is responsible for whatever the

00:07:28.861 --> 00:07:31.349
action resulted in, and warning them

00:07:31.395 --> 00:07:33.131
to be careful when using this feature.

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:35.704
It also said this was made

00:07:35.946 --> 00:07:38.084
for educational purposes only.

00:07:38.899 --> 00:07:40.956
Yeah, okay, sure.

00:07:41.831 --> 00:07:42.957
But there was one problem

00:07:43.179 --> 00:07:44.169
for Blackshades users.

00:07:44.405 --> 00:07:46.304
You couldn't just wave a wand at

00:07:46.304 --> 00:07:48.099
someone and infect their computer

00:07:48.099 --> 00:07:49.674
with Blackshades, and no one in

00:07:49.674 --> 00:07:50.925
their right mind would install

00:07:50.925 --> 00:07:52.587
this to give some random attacker

00:07:52.597 --> 00:07:53.847
full access to their computer.

00:07:54.288 --> 00:07:56.613
So, to get Blackshades on a victim’s

00:07:56.621 --> 00:07:58.714
machine, they had to trick the victim

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:01.252
into installing it themselves, to make

00:08:01.253 --> 00:08:03.045
them think they're installing something

00:08:03.046 --> 00:08:05.442
else, and that’s tricky because you

00:08:05.443 --> 00:08:07.898
basically have to exploit another human

00:08:08.229 --> 00:08:09.771
to get it installed, which brings us

00:08:09.772 --> 00:08:11.288
into the world of social engineering,

00:08:11.288 --> 00:08:13.221
the art of tricking people into doing

00:08:13.221 --> 00:08:15.082
things they don't actually want to do.

00:08:15.807 --> 00:08:17.800
There are a 1001 ways that we can

00:08:17.813 --> 00:08:19.937
all be tricked into installing

00:08:19.945 --> 00:08:21.277
things that we don't actually want.

00:08:21.551 --> 00:08:23.081
Humans are a weak link when

00:08:23.084 --> 00:08:24.416
it comes to computer security.

00:08:24.908 --> 00:08:26.070
You might have seen some of them,

00:08:26.137 --> 00:08:27.381
obvious links; click here for

00:08:27.381 --> 00:08:28.514
a free iPhone, and you're like,

00:08:28.515 --> 00:08:30.022
yeah, nah, I’m not doing that.

00:08:30.441 --> 00:08:32.592
But sometimes it’s not so obvious.

00:08:32.847 --> 00:08:34.427
Since Blackshades can spread from

00:08:34.427 --> 00:08:36.345
a friend’s computer to yours using

00:08:36.345 --> 00:08:37.792
malicious links, it can look like

00:08:37.793 --> 00:08:39.438
it’s coming from someone you trust.

00:08:40.215 --> 00:08:42.104
They can also hide malware inside

00:08:42.368 --> 00:08:44.841
pirated software, games, or movies

00:08:45.069 --> 00:08:46.630
on peer-to-peer file-sharing sites.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:48.513
So, if you downloaded a cracked version

00:08:48.514 --> 00:08:50.054
of a video game that you didn't want

00:08:50.057 --> 00:08:51.723
to buy, Blackshades might come along

00:08:51.725 --> 00:08:53.604
for the ride and get installed with it.

00:08:54.252 --> 00:08:55.001
I should know, too.

00:08:55.001 --> 00:08:56.463
When I was a teenager I downloaded a

00:08:56.463 --> 00:08:58.928
lot of shady apps and games from shady

00:08:58.929 --> 00:09:00.317
parts of the internet, and I would

00:09:00.317 --> 00:09:02.045
constantly be dealing with infections.

00:09:02.529 --> 00:09:03.762
I didn't care because I really wanted

00:09:03.762 --> 00:09:04.858
to play the game, but eventually

00:09:04.858 --> 00:09:06.435
the infection would get so bad that

00:09:06.436 --> 00:09:08.088
I couldn't use my computer at all.

00:09:08.372 --> 00:09:09.185
Pop-ups would just

00:09:09.223 --> 00:09:10.353
constantly be showing up.

00:09:10.569 --> 00:09:12.431
The CPU would crawl to a standstill.

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:13.925
I must have been hit with malware

00:09:13.926 --> 00:09:15.859
hundreds of times when I was a teenager.

00:09:16.486 --> 00:09:18.040
But that’s what got me good at fixing

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:20.138
computers, learning how to find malware

00:09:20.171 --> 00:09:21.971
and remove it and cleaning up my computer.

00:09:22.315 --> 00:09:23.598
After a while I took pride in

00:09:23.598 --> 00:09:24.692
knowing there is no problem

00:09:24.692 --> 00:09:26.029
that I can't fix on my computer.

00:09:26.344 --> 00:09:27.314
Worst case is I could just

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:28.731
reinstall the operating system

00:09:28.732 --> 00:09:31.203
if I had to, which I did a lot.

00:09:31.371 --> 00:09:32.444
I mean, a lot, a lot.

00:09:33.212 --> 00:09:35.735
Anyway, sometimes devices you buy in the

00:09:35.736 --> 00:09:37.258
store actually come with malware on them.

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:38.449
There was a story I read once

00:09:38.449 --> 00:09:39.947
where a Chinese laptop maker

00:09:39.948 --> 00:09:41.013
was selling their laptops on

00:09:41.013 --> 00:09:43.049
Amazon that came with Windows 11.

00:09:43.425 --> 00:09:44.651
Well, the thing was the Chinese seller

00:09:44.651 --> 00:09:46.189
was trying to cut costs and didn't want

00:09:46.189 --> 00:09:48.175
to pay for Windows 11 license keys for

00:09:48.175 --> 00:09:50.245
every computer, so they found a pirated

00:09:50.246 --> 00:09:51.780
version of Windows, installed that,

00:09:51.781 --> 00:09:53.344
and shipped it with their laptops.

00:09:53.731 --> 00:09:55.175
Little did they know, the pirated

00:09:55.178 --> 00:09:57.429
version contained malware and was

00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:59.200
draining people’s crypto wallets

00:09:59.214 --> 00:10:01.116
and robbing their Steam accounts.

00:10:01.613 --> 00:10:03.214
So, you need to be really careful with

00:10:03.214 --> 00:10:04.857
what apps you install and where you

00:10:04.857 --> 00:10:06.425
get them from, because having one bad

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:08.334
app on your computer can ruin you.

00:10:09.178 --> 00:10:10.251
But even apps you vet

00:10:10.255 --> 00:10:11.507
thoroughly can turn rogue.

00:10:11.562 --> 00:10:13.472
I’ve seen some popular browser extensions

00:10:13.485 --> 00:10:15.808
get purchased by someone who had malicious

00:10:15.809 --> 00:10:17.475
intent, and then they put spyware on

00:10:17.477 --> 00:10:18.887
people’s browsers without them knowing.

00:10:19.326 --> 00:10:21.117
Or maybe someone makes a simple mobile

00:10:21.117 --> 00:10:23.545
app that’s clean and fine and free, even.

00:10:23.944 --> 00:10:26.337
But as it grows in popularity, there’s

00:10:26.346 --> 00:10:28.391
always someone that asks them, hey,

00:10:28.771 --> 00:10:30.297
I’ll give you a few thousand dollars

00:10:30.297 --> 00:10:32.050
if you can put this widget in your app.

00:10:32.117 --> 00:10:32.908
Don't worry, it’s just

00:10:32.908 --> 00:10:34.150
an advertising pixel.

00:10:34.843 --> 00:10:36.401
If someone’s making free software

00:10:36.402 --> 00:10:37.614
and suddenly get offered a few

00:10:37.615 --> 00:10:38.952
thousand dollars to add a simple

00:10:38.952 --> 00:10:41.753
advertising pixel, they might say yes.

00:10:42.504 --> 00:10:45.211
Now suddenly that app, which was clean and

00:10:45.211 --> 00:10:48.478
good, now has some malicious code in it

00:10:48.981 --> 00:10:50.784
tracking what you're doing on your phone.

00:10:51.358 --> 00:10:53.475
Stuff can sneak into our devices

00:10:53.477 --> 00:10:55.281
from all kinds of directions.

00:10:55.724 --> 00:10:56.993
It’s a war out there.

00:10:56.993 --> 00:10:58.858
[Music] Then there’s USB sticks.

00:10:58.858 --> 00:11:00.736
If you put a USB stick into a computer,

00:11:01.126 --> 00:11:02.455
Windows will look at it and see if there’s

00:11:02.457 --> 00:11:05.258
a file called autorun.inf, and if so,

00:11:05.258 --> 00:11:07.008
it’ll run the commands in that file.

00:11:07.259 --> 00:11:08.575
So, if someone swings by your

00:11:08.575 --> 00:11:10.201
computer, pops a USB stick in the

00:11:10.202 --> 00:11:12.812
slot, it may auto-infect that machine.

00:11:13.643 --> 00:11:14.928
Then you could pull the USB stick

00:11:14.929 --> 00:11:16.364
out, and nobody knows what happened.

00:11:16.943 --> 00:11:18.812
Back in the days of Windows XP and Vista,

00:11:18.831 --> 00:11:21.500
this feature was on by default in Windows.

00:11:21.865 --> 00:11:23.852
Nowadays the Autorun feature is not

00:11:23.867 --> 00:11:25.837
on by default, thank goodness, but

00:11:25.837 --> 00:11:27.194
this was a popular way people would

00:11:27.194 --> 00:11:28.816
infect computers with Blackshades,

00:11:28.822 --> 00:11:30.482
since it was just dead simple to do.

00:11:30.485 --> 00:11:32.386
Just stick the USB stick in for a few

00:11:32.387 --> 00:11:33.699
seconds and pull it out, and you're done.

00:11:34.559 --> 00:11:36.007
I think the most popular way people

00:11:36.007 --> 00:11:37.939
were getting victims to install

00:11:37.939 --> 00:11:39.903
this is to send them a message

00:11:39.903 --> 00:11:41.764
saying, ‘Oh my god, is this you?

00:11:41.864 --> 00:11:43.640
How embarrassing!’ with a

00:11:43.646 --> 00:11:45.372
link to a photo or a video.

00:11:46.213 --> 00:11:48.217
Except it wasn't a photo or video.

00:11:48.233 --> 00:11:49.544
It’d look like it, but when you tried

00:11:49.545 --> 00:11:51.260
to open it, it was really a program

00:11:51.571 --> 00:11:53.266
that would install Blackshades.

00:11:53.973 --> 00:11:55.223
Another one, which I’ve actually

00:11:55.223 --> 00:11:56.465
seen in my own inbox, was something

00:11:56.467 --> 00:11:57.929
like, ‘We’ve tried to deliver a

00:11:57.929 --> 00:11:59.454
package to you three times now.

00:11:59.613 --> 00:12:00.660
We were unsuccessful.

00:12:00.866 --> 00:12:02.240
We're gonna send it back to the shipper

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.881
unless you click here.’ I always have

00:12:04.881 --> 00:12:06.585
this knee-jerk reaction like, oh man,

00:12:06.587 --> 00:12:07.803
I don't want my package returned.

00:12:08.504 --> 00:12:10.693
Then I realize it’s to an e-mail I’ve

00:12:10.707 --> 00:12:12.732
never used for ordering things before.

00:12:12.776 --> 00:12:15.586
I’m like, oh, that’s a scam.

00:12:15.768 --> 00:12:16.901
They're trying to trick me.

00:12:17.469 --> 00:12:18.756
So, no matter how vigilant

00:12:18.756 --> 00:12:20.030
you are, I think we're all

00:12:20.031 --> 00:12:21.811
susceptible to phishing e-mails.

00:12:22.451 --> 00:12:23.515
It just has to be clever

00:12:23.515 --> 00:12:24.620
enough to make you click.

00:12:25.488 --> 00:12:27.418
Once Blackshades got installed

00:12:27.418 --> 00:12:29.098
on a victim’s computer, the

00:12:29.112 --> 00:12:31.376
operator needed no skill at all.

00:12:31.559 --> 00:12:32.926
You didn't even have to open a terminal.

00:12:32.945 --> 00:12:34.180
It came with a slick, little

00:12:34.180 --> 00:12:36.211
dashboard to show you every computer

00:12:36.213 --> 00:12:38.392
that you've infected, with icons

00:12:38.393 --> 00:12:39.800
telling you if there is a camera

00:12:39.827 --> 00:12:41.640
available on that computer or not.

00:12:42.288 --> 00:12:43.559
If you were the operator, you could

00:12:43.559 --> 00:12:45.167
simply point and click on the computer

00:12:45.167 --> 00:12:47.401
you wanted to see, and now you could see

00:12:47.403 --> 00:12:50.590
their desktop, files, and yeah, camera.

00:12:51.076 --> 00:12:52.395
I mean, you could see it all;

00:12:52.396 --> 00:12:53.900
people’s private messages, social

00:12:53.901 --> 00:12:55.266
media accounts, Google searches.

00:12:55.477 --> 00:12:56.377
It was spooky.

00:12:56.556 --> 00:12:58.379
[Music] There was this guy named

00:12:58.389 --> 00:13:00.876
Stefan Rigo from Leeds in the UK

00:13:01.034 --> 00:13:02.319
who saw what Blackshades could

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:03.762
do, and he became interested.

00:13:03.778 --> 00:13:04.974
He was thirty-four years old.

00:13:05.177 --> 00:13:06.541
He bought it for forty bucks

00:13:06.637 --> 00:13:08.671
using his ex-girlfriend’s credit

00:13:08.672 --> 00:13:11.457
card, and then he infected his

00:13:11.457 --> 00:13:13.255
ex-girlfriend with this malware.

00:13:13.905 --> 00:13:15.737
Maybe he sent her a phishing chat

00:13:15.737 --> 00:13:18.192
message or plugged in a USB stick

00:13:18.199 --> 00:13:20.055
when he visited her house one day

00:13:20.056 --> 00:13:21.198
and she left the room or something.

00:13:21.567 --> 00:13:23.330
But when he was at his computer, he

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:25.815
could see when her computer was online.

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:28.901
Her computer had a camera on it,

00:13:29.209 --> 00:13:30.820
and from the dark comfort of his

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:33.266
own house, he turned on her camera

00:13:33.599 --> 00:13:35.261
and watched her in her bedroom.

00:13:36.045 --> 00:13:38.260
He found it incredibly addicting.

00:13:38.603 --> 00:13:41.021
She had no idea he was watching her.

00:13:41.661 --> 00:13:43.308
Usually there’s a little light that

00:13:43.309 --> 00:13:44.949
comes on when your camera is on, right?

00:13:45.424 --> 00:13:46.612
Well, Blackshades made sure

00:13:46.613 --> 00:13:47.916
that light didn't come on.

00:13:48.505 --> 00:13:49.301
Watching her in her

00:13:49.303 --> 00:13:51.500
bedroom gave him a rush.

00:13:51.745 --> 00:13:52.496
He liked it.

00:13:52.641 --> 00:13:54.097
He had some other lady friends and

00:13:54.097 --> 00:13:56.019
wondered what they were doing, too.

00:13:56.568 --> 00:13:58.372
So, he started infecting more and more

00:13:58.375 --> 00:14:00.752
women that he knew with Blackshades.

00:14:01.189 --> 00:14:02.640
He could hear conversations

00:14:02.659 --> 00:14:03.400
people were having.

00:14:03.719 --> 00:14:05.010
He watched them get undressed.

00:14:05.435 --> 00:14:06.997
Of course, he’s taking screenshots of

00:14:06.997 --> 00:14:08.791
them changing and saving the recordings.

00:14:08.947 --> 00:14:10.776
He liked that kind of stuff the most.

00:14:11.106 --> 00:14:12.963
Stefan got seriously addicted

00:14:12.964 --> 00:14:14.603
to watching what women do in

00:14:14.604 --> 00:14:16.267
the privacy of their own homes.

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:18.192
Every day he would open up his

00:14:18.193 --> 00:14:20.061
Blackshades dashboard and look to see

00:14:20.061 --> 00:14:22.120
what computers he infected were online,

00:14:22.664 --> 00:14:24.625
and then he’d double-click on one and

00:14:24.627 --> 00:14:26.642
sit there, watching what they were doing.

00:14:27.236 --> 00:14:28.385
Not only was he watching through

00:14:28.385 --> 00:14:29.211
the cameras, but when they'd

00:14:29.211 --> 00:14:30.394
use their computers, he’d watch

00:14:30.395 --> 00:14:31.643
what they were doing on it, too.

00:14:31.846 --> 00:14:33.545
He could see their passwords, their

00:14:33.547 --> 00:14:35.384
private messages with people, their

00:14:35.393 --> 00:14:37.743
photos, what they bought online,

00:14:37.859 --> 00:14:39.359
their online banking activity,

00:14:39.865 --> 00:14:41.776
everything they did on that computer.

00:14:42.771 --> 00:14:44.138
The thing that made it addicting

00:14:44.138 --> 00:14:45.803
to him was that he never knew

00:14:45.803 --> 00:14:46.885
when something interesting would

00:14:46.893 --> 00:14:48.496
happen or what would happen.

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:50.707
To him it was like a wave of

00:14:50.709 --> 00:14:52.581
excitement when he actually saw

00:14:52.586 --> 00:14:54.273
someone changing in front of a camera.

00:14:54.722 --> 00:14:55.710
That would make it all

00:14:55.718 --> 00:14:56.857
worth the time to him.

00:14:57.712 --> 00:14:59.129
He started out by putting it on the

00:14:59.129 --> 00:15:01.875
computers of women he knew, but then

00:15:01.888 --> 00:15:03.296
he learned how to spread it from

00:15:03.305 --> 00:15:05.416
those computers to their friends’

00:15:05.416 --> 00:15:07.869
computers, and now he was infecting

00:15:07.875 --> 00:15:08.967
other women that he didn't even

00:15:08.968 --> 00:15:10.628
know, and he didn't stop there.

00:15:10.629 --> 00:15:11.668
He was trying to infect other

00:15:11.669 --> 00:15:13.270
women, too, like people working

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:15.302
in coffee shops or at a library.

00:15:15.589 --> 00:15:16.923
It was real easy for him just

00:15:16.924 --> 00:15:18.310
to put in a USB drive and try

00:15:18.312 --> 00:15:19.487
to infect someone’s laptop.

00:15:20.467 --> 00:15:22.142
He was seriously addicted to this,

00:15:22.142 --> 00:15:24.079
and over time he got over a dozen

00:15:24.105 --> 00:15:26.232
people infected with Blackshades.

00:15:27.432 --> 00:15:29.042
With that, there was always

00:15:29.051 --> 00:15:30.599
someone online doing something

00:15:30.601 --> 00:15:32.178
interesting that he liked watching.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:36.306
There’s a whole voyeurism fetish

00:15:36.312 --> 00:15:37.133
out there on the internet.

00:15:37.145 --> 00:15:39.561
People will secretly film women getting

00:15:39.562 --> 00:15:41.337
undressed and posting it online.

00:15:41.735 --> 00:15:42.907
Or maybe they’ll hold a camera

00:15:42.908 --> 00:15:44.207
under some lady’s skirt and take

00:15:44.207 --> 00:15:45.438
a photo of that and share it.

00:15:46.056 --> 00:15:48.185
Well, this voyeurism community was

00:15:48.193 --> 00:15:50.015
hearing about what you could do with

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:52.701
Blackshades, and they were into it.

00:15:53.046 --> 00:15:54.967
The Blackshades RAT had incredible

00:15:54.969 --> 00:15:57.065
potential for secretly getting videos

00:15:57.065 --> 00:15:59.333
of women undressing or having sex.

00:15:59.805 --> 00:16:01.679
Soon the biggest user base of Blackshades

00:16:01.696 --> 00:16:03.910
were guys spying on girls to see them

00:16:03.911 --> 00:16:06.310
naked, and in most cases the guys were

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:08.228
spying on the girls they knew, keeping

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:10.310
tabs on exes, getting dirt on someone

00:16:10.310 --> 00:16:12.302
they're jealous of, or just spying on

00:16:12.302 --> 00:16:13.876
women because they found it fascinating.

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:17.068
Over time, thousands of Blackshades users

00:16:17.117 --> 00:16:19.826
were using this tool to spy on women.

00:16:20.309 --> 00:16:21.601
It really helped Blackshades

00:16:21.621 --> 00:16:22.741
grow in popularity.

00:16:23.395 --> 00:16:24.371
But they weren't the only people

00:16:24.371 --> 00:16:25.329
interested in Blackshades.

00:16:25.608 --> 00:16:27.564
It was also used to target activists.

00:16:27.743 --> 00:16:29.242
In 2012, Syria was in the

00:16:29.242 --> 00:16:30.313
middle of a civil war.

00:16:30.584 --> 00:16:31.814
People were really upset with

00:16:31.814 --> 00:16:33.236
the president of Syria, Bashar

00:16:33.248 --> 00:16:35.161
al-Assad, for using chemical

00:16:35.163 --> 00:16:36.684
weapons on his own civilians.

00:16:36.887 --> 00:16:38.626
The country ignited in large-scale

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:40.534
protest and pro-democracy rallies

00:16:40.536 --> 00:16:41.827
as part of the Arab Spring.

00:16:42.247 --> 00:16:43.834
In the midst of this, researchers at

00:16:43.834 --> 00:16:45.512
the Electronic Frontier Foundation and

00:16:45.512 --> 00:16:47.264
the Citizen Lab noticed that Syrian

00:16:47.297 --> 00:16:49.464
activists were getting hit with malware.

00:16:50.001 --> 00:16:52.084
They would get a link from a Skype account

00:16:52.352 --> 00:16:54.538
from someone they knew and trusted without

00:16:54.538 --> 00:16:56.954
realizing that account was compromised.

00:16:57.328 --> 00:16:59.597
One message read, ‘There’s a person who

00:16:59.597 --> 00:17:01.251
hates you, and he keeps talking about you.

00:17:01.424 --> 00:17:03.125
Here's a screenshot of the conversation.’

00:17:03.473 --> 00:17:05.651
There was a link to the malicious file,

00:17:06.197 --> 00:17:08.256
and when they’d click it, Blackshades

00:17:08.270 --> 00:17:10.030
would install itself on their device.

00:17:10.482 --> 00:17:12.399
[Music] The Syrian government used

00:17:12.411 --> 00:17:14.529
Blackshades to spy on opposition

00:17:14.593 --> 00:17:16.699
activists and tried to suppress them by

00:17:16.709 --> 00:17:18.631
having total control of their computers.

00:17:19.154 --> 00:17:20.129
They could do things like get

00:17:20.141 --> 00:17:21.681
information on the next rally or

00:17:21.681 --> 00:17:23.318
delete social media accounts or

00:17:23.318 --> 00:17:24.825
look through photos and documents.

00:17:25.465 --> 00:17:26.478
Before Blackshades there was

00:17:26.479 --> 00:17:27.997
another tool called DarkComet.

00:17:28.355 --> 00:17:29.991
It was developed back in 2008 by a

00:17:29.992 --> 00:17:31.801
French programmer named Jean-Pierre

00:17:31.809 --> 00:17:34.596
Lesueur, also known as DarkCoderSc.

00:17:34.629 --> 00:17:36.106
He discontinued the program

00:17:36.108 --> 00:17:37.640
partially due to its use in the

00:17:37.650 --> 00:17:39.718
Syrian civil war and possibly due

00:17:39.719 --> 00:17:41.996
to the fear of him being arrested.

00:17:42.324 --> 00:17:44.197
Like Blackshades, DarkComet was used to

00:17:44.198 --> 00:17:46.068
spy on victims through key-logging, screen

00:17:46.071 --> 00:17:48.028
captures, and by stealing their passwords.

00:17:48.621 --> 00:17:50.207
To me, this is really fascinating because

00:17:50.436 --> 00:17:52.301
at the time, a lot of activists within

00:17:52.592 --> 00:17:54.655
the hacker group Anonymous were very

00:17:54.659 --> 00:17:56.456
active in the Arab Spring trying to help

00:17:56.459 --> 00:17:58.446
the protesters from afar by knocking the

00:17:58.446 --> 00:17:59.870
government offline and doing stuff like

00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:01.966
that, and it’s wild that the very people

00:18:02.187 --> 00:18:04.407
who wanted to assist the protesters

00:18:04.731 --> 00:18:06.443
are also the ones who are accidentally

00:18:06.449 --> 00:18:08.169
assisting the government to suppress the

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:10.791
protesters, because tools are typically

00:18:10.792 --> 00:18:12.712
neutral and can be used by either side.

00:18:13.013 --> 00:18:14.788
When you make something so effective,

00:18:15.055 --> 00:18:16.484
people will notice it on both sides

00:18:16.484 --> 00:18:17.929
and use it for their own agenda.

00:18:18.389 --> 00:18:19.892
I don't have any knowledge of whether the

00:18:19.893 --> 00:18:21.662
creators of DarkComet or Blackshades were

00:18:21.662 --> 00:18:23.527
members of Anonymous, and it wouldn't

00:18:23.527 --> 00:18:24.805
surprise me if they were, because,

00:18:25.073 --> 00:18:27.312
well, at least the maker of DarkComet

00:18:27.341 --> 00:18:29.013
said some stuff online that looked a

00:18:29.014 --> 00:18:30.821
lot like what the Anonymous activists

00:18:30.826 --> 00:18:32.250
were saying about Syria at the time.

00:18:32.887 --> 00:18:34.571
So, this was yet another thing

00:18:34.614 --> 00:18:36.176
this malware was being used for.

00:18:36.384 --> 00:18:38.665
A $40 piece of software marketed to

00:18:38.665 --> 00:18:41.049
suspicious spouses and parents was being

00:18:41.049 --> 00:18:43.127
used to find dissidents during a war.

00:18:43.631 --> 00:18:45.131
Which, by the way, government intelligence

00:18:45.131 --> 00:18:47.288
units love using off-the-shelf tools

00:18:47.288 --> 00:18:49.041
to conduct their spying, since they

00:18:49.042 --> 00:18:50.154
don't have to burn any of their

00:18:50.155 --> 00:18:51.853
trade craft to conduct their tasks.

00:18:52.151 --> 00:18:54.104
A $40 off-the-shelf tool is way

00:18:54.104 --> 00:18:55.232
cheaper than spending a lot of

00:18:55.235 --> 00:18:56.529
time and energy developing their

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:57.951
own tool to do the same thing.

00:18:58.618 --> 00:19:00.195
By this time Blackshades was becoming

00:19:00.485 --> 00:19:02.193
well known in the hacker communities.

00:19:02.193 --> 00:19:03.547
Hundreds of people were buying it

00:19:03.757 --> 00:19:05.362
and infecting thousands of machines

00:19:05.362 --> 00:19:07.455
with it, which also meant the victims

00:19:07.456 --> 00:19:09.231
were waking up to the nightmare

00:19:09.234 --> 00:19:10.683
happening to their computers.

00:19:10.912 --> 00:19:13.312
Victims would often get extortion e-mails

00:19:13.313 --> 00:19:15.042
where they would receive an embarrassing

00:19:15.042 --> 00:19:17.590
photo of them with some kind of demand.

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:19.367
The obvious demand is to pay

00:19:19.367 --> 00:19:21.039
some Bitcoin and we’ll delete

00:19:21.040 --> 00:19:23.332
it, but some were downright evil.

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:25.123
Like, people would send a half-naked

00:19:25.126 --> 00:19:27.429
photo to their victim and say, ‘Send

00:19:27.431 --> 00:19:29.869
me a fully-nude photo or I’m posting

00:19:29.871 --> 00:19:31.918
this on your own social media account.

00:19:32.305 --> 00:19:33.394
Let me show you that I have

00:19:33.395 --> 00:19:34.978
access to it.’ Then they would

00:19:34.978 --> 00:19:36.751
post a test message to prove it.

00:19:37.390 --> 00:19:40.629
It would rattle a lot of these women, and

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:42.029
they would sometimes send the pictures

00:19:42.033 --> 00:19:44.230
that were demanded simply out of fear.

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:46.369
[Music] Sometimes the attacker would

00:19:46.369 --> 00:19:47.761
catch a picture of their victim

00:19:47.886 --> 00:19:49.944
having sex and send them a picture

00:19:49.945 --> 00:19:52.358
of that and demand a video call over

00:19:52.358 --> 00:19:54.341
Skype, and they'd ask the women to

00:19:54.341 --> 00:19:56.949
do a five-minute sex show for them on

00:19:56.950 --> 00:19:59.695
camera as part of the ransom demand.

00:20:00.312 --> 00:20:01.556
If they didn't do it, the attacker

00:20:01.559 --> 00:20:02.934
had access to all their social media

00:20:02.935 --> 00:20:04.995
accounts and said they'd post something

00:20:04.995 --> 00:20:06.594
really terrible if they didn't to it.

00:20:07.272 --> 00:20:09.436
Blackshades was a growing problem,

00:20:09.710 --> 00:20:11.045
and victims were being almost

00:20:11.056 --> 00:20:13.156
entirely silent about the matter due

00:20:13.158 --> 00:20:14.864
to all the embarrassment and fear.

00:20:15.342 --> 00:20:17.141
I hate to say it, but it’s

00:20:17.206 --> 00:20:19.046
possible that some women died

00:20:19.054 --> 00:20:20.703
by suicide because of this.

00:20:21.276 --> 00:20:22.746
I didn't see any specific stories

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:24.181
about that happening with Blackshades,

00:20:24.556 --> 00:20:27.330
but I’ve seen countless stories where

00:20:27.346 --> 00:20:29.966
online bullying and abuse and harassment

00:20:29.983 --> 00:20:32.299
has led to women feeling so desperate

00:20:32.299 --> 00:20:34.855
that they'd rather die than face the

00:20:34.855 --> 00:20:36.781
embarrassment or harassment anymore.

00:20:36.796 --> 00:20:38.293
It’s really tragic.

00:20:39.445 --> 00:20:40.925
We're gonna take a quick ad break,

00:20:40.926 --> 00:20:43.299
but stay with us because this is

00:20:43.299 --> 00:20:45.304
where the FBI starts to get involved.

00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:51.176
The FBI started rooting around in

00:20:51.176 --> 00:20:54.073
some hacker forums looking for crime,

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:56.042
but they weren't focused on this.

00:20:56.173 --> 00:20:57.296
Not yet, at least.

00:20:57.379 --> 00:20:59.655
They were focused on stuff like

00:20:59.745 --> 00:21:01.941
credit card fraud and online fraud.

00:21:02.443 --> 00:21:04.573
In 2010 the FBI decided to go

00:21:04.573 --> 00:21:06.416
on the dark web and build their

00:21:06.456 --> 00:21:08.767
own stolen credit card exchange.

00:21:09.283 --> 00:21:10.335
They were hoping thieves would

00:21:10.335 --> 00:21:11.932
come and sell stolen cards and

00:21:11.932 --> 00:21:13.571
people would buy them, and then the

00:21:13.573 --> 00:21:15.129
FBI would catch them in the act.

00:21:15.423 --> 00:21:17.360
It’s wild to me that the FBI built

00:21:17.425 --> 00:21:19.303
their own carders market on the

00:21:19.305 --> 00:21:21.956
dark web, a honeypot to trap people.

00:21:22.495 --> 00:21:24.378
Not only could you buy and sell stolen

00:21:24.378 --> 00:21:26.138
credit cards there, but they sold

00:21:26.167 --> 00:21:28.508
tools for stealing credit cards, too.

00:21:29.097 --> 00:21:31.177
However, dark web forums like this only

00:21:31.178 --> 00:21:33.557
work when there’s trust, so the FBI,

00:21:33.636 --> 00:21:36.241
which was acting like dark web operators,

00:21:36.712 --> 00:21:38.767
said they’ll verify every tool before

00:21:38.767 --> 00:21:40.399
it’s allowed to be sold on the site.

00:21:40.903 --> 00:21:42.254
So, for instance, if you wanted to sell

00:21:42.254 --> 00:21:44.715
a credit card scraper, the FBI would

00:21:44.802 --> 00:21:46.841
have to vet you as a seller first.

00:21:46.980 --> 00:21:48.399
Send us one and we’ll test it, and if

00:21:48.399 --> 00:21:49.985
it’s good, we’ll approve you as a vendor.

00:21:50.706 --> 00:21:52.444
The administrators were either

00:21:52.461 --> 00:21:54.062
undercover agents or confidential

00:21:54.062 --> 00:21:55.535
sources in the investigation.

00:21:55.926 --> 00:21:57.312
They were reviewing these products

00:21:57.318 --> 00:21:59.108
to get evidence of criminal activity

00:21:59.351 --> 00:22:00.686
and to investigate the hardware,

00:22:00.764 --> 00:22:02.329
software, and methods used.

00:22:02.648 --> 00:22:04.713
The FBI was looking for credit card

00:22:04.714 --> 00:22:07.993
fraud, but then the co-creator of

00:22:07.998 --> 00:22:10.716
Blackshades, Michael Hogue, wanted

00:22:10.716 --> 00:22:13.032
to become a vendor on this forum.

00:22:13.032 --> 00:22:15.343
[Music] So, he submitted his tool,

00:22:15.447 --> 00:22:17.581
Blackshades, to show them that

00:22:17.582 --> 00:22:19.515
he has a real tool that can be

00:22:19.516 --> 00:22:21.488
used to scrape credit card data.

00:22:22.081 --> 00:22:25.906
He had no idea he was pitching the FBI.

00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:28.206
It’s kind of ironic that the

00:22:28.207 --> 00:22:29.818
co-creator of Blackshades fell for

00:22:29.818 --> 00:22:31.538
a social engineering trap himself.

00:22:31.973 --> 00:22:32.269
See?

00:22:32.275 --> 00:22:33.780
Even he’s susceptible to that.

00:22:34.426 --> 00:22:35.915
The FBI couldn't believe

00:22:35.974 --> 00:22:37.618
Michael sent them his malware.

00:22:37.963 --> 00:22:40.341
This was clear evidence of his intent,

00:22:40.573 --> 00:22:42.670
to sell Blackshades to criminals.

00:22:43.210 --> 00:22:44.912
All that language that this was

00:22:44.912 --> 00:22:46.538
only for educational purposes

00:22:46.539 --> 00:22:48.137
or for a parent to monitor their

00:22:48.137 --> 00:22:49.978
kid wasn't gonna fly anymore.

00:22:50.205 --> 00:22:51.782
When you're selling it to criminals on

00:22:51.782 --> 00:22:53.598
a dark web forum to steal credit card

00:22:53.604 --> 00:22:55.885
data with, then that’s clear intent.

00:22:56.622 --> 00:22:59.185
In 2012, the trap snapped shut.

00:22:59.445 --> 00:23:01.240
The FBI ran a sting operation

00:23:01.242 --> 00:23:02.995
called Operation Card Shop.

00:23:03.276 --> 00:23:04.808
It led to twenty-four

00:23:04.827 --> 00:23:06.245
arrests in eight countries.

00:23:06.447 --> 00:23:07.805
Almost all of these arrests

00:23:07.805 --> 00:23:09.520
were for credit card fraud,

00:23:09.980 --> 00:23:11.158
but there was one exception.

00:23:11.369 --> 00:23:13.504
One of the people arrested was Michael

00:23:13.513 --> 00:23:15.603
Hogue, the maker of Blackshades.

00:23:15.880 --> 00:23:17.397
He was charged under the Computer

00:23:17.399 --> 00:23:19.068
Fraud and Abuse Act for conspiracy

00:23:19.068 --> 00:23:20.492
to commit computer hacking

00:23:20.743 --> 00:23:22.150
and transmission of malware.

00:23:22.578 --> 00:23:24.487
Writing and selling software isn't

00:23:24.532 --> 00:23:26.136
illegal, but writing and selling

00:23:26.136 --> 00:23:27.751
software with the intent of logging

00:23:27.758 --> 00:23:29.477
keystrokes, ransomwaring files,

00:23:29.487 --> 00:23:31.115
stealing credit cards, and spying on

00:23:31.121 --> 00:23:34.360
webcams without consent is illegal.

00:23:35.211 --> 00:23:37.541
Hogue cooperated with investigators,

00:23:38.217 --> 00:23:40.825
which meant he avoided prison entirely.

00:23:41.225 --> 00:23:42.541
He was sentenced to five years of

00:23:42.541 --> 00:23:44.353
probation and he was ordered to

00:23:44.353 --> 00:23:47.767
forfeit $40,000, and had to perform

00:23:47.772 --> 00:23:49.877
500 hours of community service.

00:23:50.707 --> 00:23:51.455
So, that’s it, right?

00:23:52.264 --> 00:23:53.851
Co-creator of Blackshades arrested,

00:23:54.116 --> 00:23:56.118
2,000 people in cuffs, game over

00:23:56.154 --> 00:23:57.530
for Blackshades at least, right?

00:23:58.078 --> 00:23:59.015
Except it wasn't.

00:23:59.304 --> 00:24:01.231
The Blackshades website stayed up

00:24:01.309 --> 00:24:03.006
and operational and kept selling

00:24:03.007 --> 00:24:04.437
it to people for forty bucks.

00:24:04.972 --> 00:24:06.422
What's hilarious is around that

00:24:06.423 --> 00:24:07.749
time, Blackshades became so

00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:09.746
popular that you could find pirated

00:24:09.747 --> 00:24:11.152
versions of it floating around, too.

00:24:11.393 --> 00:24:12.991
People who didn't want to pay the $40

00:24:12.992 --> 00:24:14.712
could download it and install a pirated

00:24:14.714 --> 00:24:16.689
version and use it, and it’s hilarious

00:24:16.692 --> 00:24:19.745
because almost certainly a pirated

00:24:19.749 --> 00:24:22.720
version of Blackshades is going to come

00:24:22.720 --> 00:24:24.808
with some other malware bundled on it.

00:24:24.808 --> 00:24:26.535
You're gonna get some other spy

00:24:26.535 --> 00:24:28.734
tool installed if you install this.

00:24:29.539 --> 00:24:31.410
People were spying on the spies.

00:24:32.227 --> 00:24:32.986
Over the next year,

00:24:32.994 --> 00:24:34.439
Blackshades did not shrink.

00:24:34.455 --> 00:24:35.235
It grew.

00:24:35.687 --> 00:24:38.952
In 2013 Blackshades made its news again.

00:24:39.346 --> 00:24:42.124
REPORTER: Miss Teen USA 2013, Cassidy

00:24:42.125 --> 00:24:44.300
Wolf, was one of the victims of a hacker

00:24:44.501 --> 00:24:46.360
using the malicious software called

00:24:46.373 --> 00:24:49.045
Blackshades RAT, or remote access tool.

00:24:49.313 --> 00:24:51.490
Authorities say last year a hacker

00:24:51.491 --> 00:24:54.114
used Wolf’s personal computer webcam to

00:24:54.114 --> 00:24:56.253
take nude photos of her and threatened

00:24:56.253 --> 00:24:58.238
to post them online if Wolf didn't

00:24:58.241 --> 00:25:00.088
send him more revealing photos.

00:25:00.333 --> 00:25:02.092
Instead, she went to police.

00:25:02.495 --> 00:25:03.850
JACK: Cassidy Wolf, a high-school

00:25:03.851 --> 00:25:05.553
student from Temecula, California,

00:25:05.640 --> 00:25:07.121
got an anonymous e-mail.

00:25:07.637 --> 00:25:09.751
A stranger said he had photos of

00:25:09.752 --> 00:25:11.680
her, photos taken in her bedroom

00:25:11.977 --> 00:25:13.591
through her webcam, on her own

00:25:13.591 --> 00:25:15.221
computer after he hacked into it.

00:25:15.558 --> 00:25:17.973
He tried to extort her after threatening

00:25:17.975 --> 00:25:20.202
to release intimate photos unless she

00:25:20.202 --> 00:25:23.015
provided him with a special performance.

00:25:23.294 --> 00:25:24.805
Classic sextortion.

00:25:24.805 --> 00:25:27.030
[Music] She had no idea

00:25:27.074 --> 00:25:28.087
she was infected by this.

00:25:28.097 --> 00:25:29.901
She said her camera light never came

00:25:29.903 --> 00:25:31.507
on, and she didn't know anybody had

00:25:31.507 --> 00:25:33.069
been staring at her in her room this

00:25:33.069 --> 00:25:34.876
whole time or watching her computer.

00:25:35.468 --> 00:25:36.963
She didn't send any

00:25:37.108 --> 00:25:38.583
photos to this stranger.

00:25:38.886 --> 00:25:40.693
She went to law enforcement instead.

00:25:41.235 --> 00:25:43.565
The FBI ran the investigation, and when

00:25:43.565 --> 00:25:45.434
they figured out who was behind it, it

00:25:45.435 --> 00:25:47.536
turned out the hacker wasn't some shadowy

00:25:47.536 --> 00:25:49.062
figure on the far side of the world.

00:25:49.565 --> 00:25:51.331
It was a guy she went to high school

00:25:51.331 --> 00:25:53.742
with, a former classmate named Jared

00:25:53.764 --> 00:25:56.418
Abrahams, and she was not the only one.

00:25:56.773 --> 00:25:59.086
Jared used Blackshades to break

00:25:59.101 --> 00:26:00.496
into the computers of at least

00:26:00.529 --> 00:26:02.417
two dozen women and girls.

00:26:02.783 --> 00:26:03.976
Their ages ranged from

00:26:03.976 --> 00:26:05.684
sixteen to the early twenties.

00:26:06.308 --> 00:26:08.546
Jared got arrested by the FBI.

00:26:09.152 --> 00:26:10.964
Two months later he pled guilty

00:26:10.965 --> 00:26:12.663
to extortion and hacking.

00:26:13.257 --> 00:26:14.829
He went to court for sentencing

00:26:15.381 --> 00:26:16.919
and he was sentenced to eighteen

00:26:16.919 --> 00:26:17.977
months in federal prison.

00:26:19.171 --> 00:26:21.066
Four months after this extortion

00:26:21.066 --> 00:26:22.797
attempt, Cassidy Wolf was

00:26:22.802 --> 00:26:25.833
crowed Miss Teen USA 2013.

00:26:26.471 --> 00:26:28.056
Instead of keeping quiet about what

00:26:28.066 --> 00:26:29.937
happened to her, she did the opposite.

00:26:29.956 --> 00:26:31.934
She spent her year using that title to

00:26:31.951 --> 00:26:34.499
go to schools and talk about exactly

00:26:34.501 --> 00:26:38.095
that, webcam hacking and sextortion.

00:26:38.731 --> 00:26:40.514
CASSIDY: Yeah, so, a few years ago

00:26:40.544 --> 00:26:42.789
I was with a friend of mine, and I

00:26:42.790 --> 00:26:44.886
randomly got an e-mail, and in that

00:26:44.916 --> 00:26:46.879
e-mail he had attached photos that

00:26:46.879 --> 00:26:48.596
he had taken of me through my webcam.

00:26:49.176 --> 00:26:50.827
So, it ended up being a

00:26:51.126 --> 00:26:52.404
federal investigation…

00:26:52.405 --> 00:26:52.662
INTERVIEWER: Yeah.

00:26:52.683 --> 00:26:53.628
CASSIDY: …for three months straight.

00:26:54.400 --> 00:26:55.786
The guy that did it ended up going

00:26:55.787 --> 00:26:57.218
to prison for eighteen months.

00:26:57.679 --> 00:26:58.929
JACK: Wow, how brave of her to

00:26:58.930 --> 00:27:00.421
use her newfound popularity to

00:27:00.421 --> 00:27:02.381
fight for justice and to win.

00:27:02.811 --> 00:27:04.639
So, that’s one guy caught for spying

00:27:04.640 --> 00:27:06.809
on girls, but that didn't slow down

00:27:06.809 --> 00:27:08.444
the continual growth of Blackshades’

00:27:08.460 --> 00:27:10.843
sale and usage, because by May

00:27:10.856 --> 00:27:13.703
2014, Blackshades was booming.

00:27:14.130 --> 00:27:15.870
By then it had infected over

00:27:15.870 --> 00:27:18.041
a million computers worldwide.

00:27:18.705 --> 00:27:20.053
[Music] When the FBI arrested

00:27:20.113 --> 00:27:21.393
Blackshades’ co-creator, Michael

00:27:21.393 --> 00:27:23.706
Hogue, he became a cooperating witness,

00:27:24.124 --> 00:27:26.251
which meant he let them see all the

00:27:26.251 --> 00:27:28.128
inside baseball of his organization.

00:27:28.345 --> 00:27:29.425
He showed the FBI how many

00:27:29.425 --> 00:27:30.957
computers it had infected, who

00:27:30.957 --> 00:27:32.107
the users were, everything.

00:27:32.652 --> 00:27:33.913
Well, actually, I don't know how

00:27:33.913 --> 00:27:35.669
much he actually showed them versus

00:27:35.670 --> 00:27:37.148
how much they saw, because they

00:27:37.149 --> 00:27:38.995
just seized all his servers and took

00:27:38.995 --> 00:27:40.250
all the computers for themselves.

00:27:40.441 --> 00:27:41.943
So, the FBI knew the malware had

00:27:41.944 --> 00:27:43.750
infected over 500,000 computers in

00:27:43.750 --> 00:27:45.595
over a hundred countries and had

00:27:45.598 --> 00:27:48.545
generated over $350,000 in sales.

00:27:49.123 --> 00:27:50.879
They had the names and addresses of more

00:27:50.879 --> 00:27:54.149
than 6,000 customer accounts, basically

00:27:54.149 --> 00:27:55.675
a customer list of all the people

00:27:55.676 --> 00:27:57.557
around the world who bought Blackshades.

00:27:58.151 --> 00:27:59.601
They shared this list with law

00:27:59.616 --> 00:28:01.344
enforcement partners around the world.

00:28:02.017 --> 00:28:04.113
So, what do you do as the FBI when

00:28:04.115 --> 00:28:05.596
you have the billing information for

00:28:05.597 --> 00:28:07.411
thousands of Blackshades customers?

00:28:07.904 --> 00:28:08.702
I know you've heard the term

00:28:08.704 --> 00:28:10.150
before; they can't arrest us all.

00:28:10.468 --> 00:28:11.259
But can they?

00:28:11.606 --> 00:28:12.631
I think they wanted to.

00:28:13.111 --> 00:28:15.381
But the FBI has a 99% conviction rate.

00:28:15.583 --> 00:28:16.860
If they arrest someone, they better

00:28:16.861 --> 00:28:18.204
have bulletproof evidence that

00:28:18.204 --> 00:28:19.679
that person committed a crime.

00:28:20.293 --> 00:28:21.613
I mean, that one user, Stefan,

00:28:21.899 --> 00:28:22.827
bought the thing using his

00:28:22.887 --> 00:28:24.553
ex-girlfriend’s credit card, right?

00:28:24.962 --> 00:28:26.300
So, just in the list of names of

00:28:26.309 --> 00:28:27.936
people who purchased it isn't enough.

00:28:28.305 --> 00:28:30.485
They need to go through each customer

00:28:30.485 --> 00:28:31.747
individually and prove that they

00:28:31.750 --> 00:28:33.060
were actually abusing the tool.

00:28:33.373 --> 00:28:34.509
Because what if someone’s just using

00:28:34.509 --> 00:28:35.871
it to monitor their child’s computer

00:28:35.871 --> 00:28:38.446
activity like the website advertised it?

00:28:38.788 --> 00:28:40.252
They didn't want to make any mistakes.

00:28:40.708 --> 00:28:43.049
So, they spent months and an enormous

00:28:43.051 --> 00:28:45.207
amount of time building cases for

00:28:45.208 --> 00:28:47.426
as many of its users as they could.

00:28:48.273 --> 00:28:49.971
They were able to get enough evidence

00:28:49.971 --> 00:28:51.864
on lots of people who were clearly

00:28:51.881 --> 00:28:54.034
abusing the tool, but those people

00:28:54.034 --> 00:28:56.199
were located all over the world, so

00:28:56.200 --> 00:28:57.561
they reached out to law enforcement in

00:28:57.561 --> 00:28:59.197
eighteen different countries to try to

00:28:59.197 --> 00:29:02.395
do a worldwide coordinated takedown.

00:29:03.315 --> 00:29:06.341
On May 19th, 2014, law enforcement

00:29:06.368 --> 00:29:08.109
officials from around the world

00:29:08.109 --> 00:29:10.426
raided the homes of Blackshade users,

00:29:10.728 --> 00:29:12.966
arresting as many people as they could.

00:29:13.473 --> 00:29:15.523
Here's Preet Bharara, the US Attorney for

00:29:15.523 --> 00:29:16.962
the Southern District of New York, in a

00:29:16.964 --> 00:29:18.918
press conference explaining what they did.

00:29:19.374 --> 00:29:21.259
PREET: We are announcing another global

00:29:21.259 --> 00:29:23.201
law enforcement operation that has

00:29:23.203 --> 00:29:26.508
exposed and crippled a frightening form of

00:29:26.508 --> 00:29:29.588
cybercrime affecting hundreds of thousands

00:29:29.605 --> 00:29:31.810
of computer users around the world.

00:29:32.262 --> 00:29:33.974
JACK: The operation led to ninety-seven

00:29:33.980 --> 00:29:36.464
arrests and 359 searches across the

00:29:36.464 --> 00:29:38.838
world, with people detained in the US,

00:29:38.878 --> 00:29:41.416
the UK, Germany, France, the Netherlands,

00:29:41.426 --> 00:29:42.867
Belgium, Austria, Switzerland,

00:29:42.878 --> 00:29:44.735
Italy, Croatia, Denmark, Estonia,

00:29:44.739 --> 00:29:46.752
Finland, Moldova, Canada, and Chile.

00:29:47.301 --> 00:29:48.623
The age of the criminals varied.

00:29:48.629 --> 00:29:50.867
Some were teenagers; a sixteen-year-old in

00:29:50.869 --> 00:29:52.690
the UK, a seventeen-year-old in Finland,

00:29:52.895 --> 00:29:54.354
an eighteen-year-old in the Netherlands.

00:29:54.591 --> 00:29:56.478
Others were adults, and I’m pretty

00:29:56.479 --> 00:29:58.639
sure it was all males who got arrested.

00:29:58.701 --> 00:30:01.667
Ninety-seven people

00:30:01.995 --> 00:30:03.588
arrested for using the tool.

00:30:04.098 --> 00:30:05.919
The reasons for using it varied, too.

00:30:05.951 --> 00:30:08.303
Some used it for voyeurism and extortion.

00:30:08.529 --> 00:30:10.153
Some used it for financial theft.

00:30:10.375 --> 00:30:12.803
Some built botnets to launch DDoS attacks.

00:30:12.900 --> 00:30:14.673
Some locked computers up with ransomware.

00:30:15.189 --> 00:30:16.997
More than a thousand data-storage

00:30:17.003 --> 00:30:19.020
devices were also seized, and they

00:30:19.020 --> 00:30:21.352
took the Blackshades website offline.

00:30:22.163 --> 00:30:23.829
One case involved an eighteen-year-old

00:30:23.829 --> 00:30:24.935
man from the Netherlands who

00:30:24.961 --> 00:30:27.665
allegedly infected 2,000 computers

00:30:27.668 --> 00:30:29.426
to take photos of women and girls

00:30:29.748 --> 00:30:31.526
who were using their machines.

00:30:31.870 --> 00:30:34.858
2,000 infections from one guy alone.

00:30:35.788 --> 00:30:38.215
In 2014 prosecutors in the US

00:30:38.286 --> 00:30:40.699
unsealed charges against five people.

00:30:40.959 --> 00:30:42.447
Here's FBI’s Special Agent

00:30:42.460 --> 00:30:43.777
in charge, Leo Taddeo.

00:30:44.318 --> 00:30:46.060
LEO: [Music] We have charged three key

00:30:46.060 --> 00:30:48.126
members of the Blackshades organization,

00:30:48.625 --> 00:30:50.188
as well as two cybercriminals in

00:30:50.188 --> 00:30:52.141
the New York area who purchased the

00:30:52.141 --> 00:30:54.012
software and used it to victimize

00:30:54.289 --> 00:30:56.190
hundreds of innocent people.

00:30:56.987 --> 00:30:57.931
Specifically we announce

00:30:57.936 --> 00:30:59.601
charges against the two alleged

00:30:59.617 --> 00:31:01.681
creators of the Blackshades RAT,

00:31:01.921 --> 00:31:04.062
Alex Yucel and Michael Hogue.

00:31:04.785 --> 00:31:07.127
Yucel, a Swedish citizen, was arrested

00:31:07.128 --> 00:31:10.387
in Moldova in November 2013, and he is

00:31:10.387 --> 00:31:12.082
awaiting extradition to the United States.

00:31:12.673 --> 00:31:13.642
The indictment against Yucel

00:31:13.652 --> 00:31:15.234
has been under seal and was

00:31:15.234 --> 00:31:16.563
made public earlier today.

00:31:17.434 --> 00:31:19.808
Mr. Hogue was arrested in Arizona

00:31:19.815 --> 00:31:22.408
in June of 2012, and subsequently

00:31:22.408 --> 00:31:25.148
pled guilty in January of 2013.

00:31:25.705 --> 00:31:27.261
Mr. Hogue has been cooperating

00:31:27.261 --> 00:31:28.463
with the government and its

00:31:28.463 --> 00:31:30.613
investigation since his arrest.

00:31:31.425 --> 00:31:32.920
We have also charged and arrested

00:31:32.921 --> 00:31:35.351
today Brendan Johnston, a former

00:31:35.355 --> 00:31:37.675
Blackshades employee who helped market

00:31:37.688 --> 00:31:40.069
and sell the RAT as well as provide

00:31:40.094 --> 00:31:41.711
technical assistance to its users,

00:31:42.204 --> 00:31:44.380
and two New York-area purchasers

00:31:44.399 --> 00:31:46.423
of the RAT who allegedly used it

00:31:46.423 --> 00:31:48.228
to steal online account information

00:31:48.551 --> 00:31:51.876
and spy on victims through webcams.

00:31:52.392 --> 00:31:53.537
JACK: When the FBI made copies

00:31:53.538 --> 00:31:54.680
of the customer list, they

00:31:54.680 --> 00:31:56.251
didn't stop at the developers.

00:31:56.335 --> 00:31:58.894
Across more than forty US cities, agents

00:31:58.907 --> 00:32:00.653
knocked on the doors of regular people

00:32:00.900 --> 00:32:03.008
who paid forty bucks, and if you were

00:32:03.009 --> 00:32:04.821
on hacking forums at the time, you would

00:32:04.822 --> 00:32:07.304
have seen panic unfold in real time.

00:32:07.657 --> 00:32:09.599
People were posting things like ‘The

00:32:09.600 --> 00:32:11.872
FBI just raided my house’ or ‘They

00:32:11.872 --> 00:32:13.895
took my computer’ or ‘What do I

00:32:13.897 --> 00:32:16.286
do?’ One guy in Canada posted that

00:32:16.287 --> 00:32:17.527
the police showed up with a warrant

00:32:17.531 --> 00:32:18.976
because his son had bought it.

00:32:19.550 --> 00:32:21.452
FBI: During this past week, FBI

00:32:21.456 --> 00:32:23.095
agents in over forty cities across

00:32:23.095 --> 00:32:24.982
the country conducted searches,

00:32:25.194 --> 00:32:27.325
interviews, and arrests of people

00:32:27.326 --> 00:32:29.121
who purchased Blackshades and may

00:32:29.124 --> 00:32:30.975
have used it to commit cybercrimes.

00:32:31.756 --> 00:32:33.478
We also passed leads to foreign law

00:32:33.478 --> 00:32:35.129
enforcement agencies around the world.

00:32:35.661 --> 00:32:37.779
In the last few days our law

00:32:37.781 --> 00:32:39.938
enforcement partners in nineteen

00:32:39.939 --> 00:32:41.482
foreign countries carried out

00:32:41.482 --> 00:32:43.069
their own law enforcement actions.

00:32:43.422 --> 00:32:45.590
The combined efforts of the FBI and

00:32:45.590 --> 00:32:48.101
foreign law enforcement marks the

00:32:48.105 --> 00:32:50.756
Blackshades takedown as one of the largest

00:32:50.801 --> 00:32:52.948
global cyber operations in history.

00:32:53.579 --> 00:32:55.197
JACK: Wow, one of the largest

00:32:55.260 --> 00:32:58.208
global cyber operations in history.

00:32:59.083 --> 00:33:00.104
Remember that guy I told you about

00:33:00.105 --> 00:33:02.169
earlier, Stefan Rigo, who infected

00:33:02.170 --> 00:33:03.707
over a dozen women with Blackshades?

00:33:03.915 --> 00:33:05.503
He was arrested in this operation,

00:33:05.503 --> 00:33:06.804
too, and he pleaded guilty.

00:33:07.140 --> 00:33:09.887
He received a suspended sentence, 200

00:33:09.923 --> 00:33:12.215
hours of community service, and seven

00:33:12.215 --> 00:33:14.163
years on the sex offender registry.

00:33:14.701 --> 00:33:16.130
FBI: Combating cybercrime is

00:33:16.131 --> 00:33:17.693
a top priority for the FBI.

00:33:18.263 --> 00:33:20.275
The charges unsealed today should put

00:33:20.297 --> 00:33:22.810
cybercriminals around the world on notice.

00:33:23.206 --> 00:33:24.781
If you think you can hide behind

00:33:24.782 --> 00:33:27.116
your computer screen, think again.

00:33:28.096 --> 00:33:29.157
Just like in the physical

00:33:29.158 --> 00:33:31.036
world, the FBI will follow the

00:33:31.041 --> 00:33:32.630
digital trail to your doorstep.

00:33:33.168 --> 00:33:34.397
If you think operating in a

00:33:34.397 --> 00:33:36.019
foreign country puts you out

00:33:36.020 --> 00:33:37.655
of our reach, think again.

00:33:38.064 --> 00:33:39.336
We have many law enforcement

00:33:39.339 --> 00:33:41.167
partners around the world who

00:33:41.167 --> 00:33:42.490
are with us in this fight.

00:33:43.212 --> 00:33:45.375
If we can't reach you, they can.

00:33:48.055 --> 00:33:49.658
JACK: Blackshades is old now.

00:33:49.669 --> 00:33:51.755
Most antivirus software can detect

00:33:51.756 --> 00:33:52.910
it, and some of the methods it

00:33:52.910 --> 00:33:54.467
used to spread no longer work.

00:33:54.702 --> 00:33:55.977
The website is gone.

00:33:55.980 --> 00:33:56.956
The forums are dead.

00:33:57.339 --> 00:33:59.202
The people who built it got arrested.

00:33:59.698 --> 00:34:00.785
But even though Blackshades

00:34:00.810 --> 00:34:02.841
today is mostly a museum piece,

00:34:03.262 --> 00:34:04.480
malware doesn't really die.

00:34:04.488 --> 00:34:05.303
It evolves.

00:34:05.488 --> 00:34:07.037
The $40 RAT with the friendly

00:34:07.039 --> 00:34:08.803
menu got replaced by newer

00:34:08.806 --> 00:34:10.029
ones with different names.

00:34:10.114 --> 00:34:11.409
The criminal economy moved

00:34:11.411 --> 00:34:12.734
into newer, more sophisticated

00:34:12.773 --> 00:34:14.766
malware that’s harder to detect.

00:34:15.152 --> 00:34:17.364
What's still true is malware wants

00:34:17.364 --> 00:34:19.282
to be sneaky and live quietly.

00:34:19.554 --> 00:34:20.592
It doesn't want the victim

00:34:20.592 --> 00:34:22.134
to know they are infected.

00:34:22.477 --> 00:34:24.556
There’s an asymmetry of knowledge

00:34:24.556 --> 00:34:26.585
here which is a huge gap, actually.

00:34:26.600 --> 00:34:28.571
Most people don't know enough about

00:34:28.572 --> 00:34:30.589
computers or how to secure them to

00:34:30.591 --> 00:34:32.966
protect themselves reliably, and these

00:34:32.967 --> 00:34:35.145
attackers rely on that lack of knowledge

00:34:35.147 --> 00:34:37.437
to hide in the wires, under the radar.

00:34:38.315 --> 00:34:39.772
Listening to shows like this

00:34:40.053 --> 00:34:41.516
starts to bridge that gap.

00:34:41.576 --> 00:34:44.197
Now you're aware that tools

00:34:44.199 --> 00:34:45.533
like this exist in the world,

00:34:45.866 --> 00:34:46.891
and they're a big deal.

00:34:47.132 --> 00:34:48.206
I mean, this one resulted

00:34:48.217 --> 00:34:49.712
in one of the largest global

00:34:49.712 --> 00:34:51.330
cyber operations in history.

00:34:51.770 --> 00:34:53.359
This isn't just some little thing.

00:34:53.360 --> 00:34:54.647
This is a huge problem.

00:34:55.062 --> 00:34:56.761
So, awareness is step

00:34:56.761 --> 00:34:58.365
number one for your safety.

00:34:58.979 --> 00:35:00.986
Be aware that messages from friends

00:35:00.988 --> 00:35:03.331
can contain malware, and it doesn't

00:35:03.331 --> 00:35:04.986
always mean that they sent it to you.

00:35:05.462 --> 00:35:06.772
It’s always good to verify things

00:35:07.024 --> 00:35:08.218
out-of-band if you're not sure.

00:35:08.220 --> 00:35:09.430
Like, if you get a text message from

00:35:09.430 --> 00:35:10.808
a friend with a suspicious link,

00:35:11.083 --> 00:35:12.156
call them on the phone and be like,

00:35:12.156 --> 00:35:13.418
hey, did you just send me this text?

00:35:13.728 --> 00:35:14.232
[Music] It’s always better

00:35:14.236 --> 00:35:15.192
to be safe than sorry.

00:35:16.036 --> 00:35:17.671
Be aware that all of the documents

00:35:17.672 --> 00:35:19.060
that you have, the photos you took,

00:35:19.265 --> 00:35:20.817
or anything you've saved on the cloud

00:35:21.351 --> 00:35:24.165
may and probably will get loose at

00:35:24.168 --> 00:35:26.534
some point and get out in the world.

00:35:26.961 --> 00:35:28.830
Data breaches are extremely common,

00:35:28.837 --> 00:35:30.481
and malware like this makes it

00:35:30.491 --> 00:35:32.509
easy for an attacker to get into

00:35:32.509 --> 00:35:33.901
your computer to see your stuff.

00:35:34.390 --> 00:35:37.063
So treat your sensitive documents and

00:35:37.064 --> 00:35:40.589
photos with much more care than normal.

00:35:41.456 --> 00:35:44.015
For me, I store stuff offline on

00:35:44.016 --> 00:35:46.138
a hard drive that’s encrypted.

00:35:46.659 --> 00:35:47.787
It’s a pain in the neck to

00:35:47.789 --> 00:35:49.058
interact with those files on

00:35:49.058 --> 00:35:50.156
there, but that’s the point.

00:35:50.175 --> 00:35:51.559
I want to make it really hard for

00:35:51.560 --> 00:35:52.984
anyone else to access it, too.

00:35:53.686 --> 00:35:55.500
There are also USB sticks that

00:35:55.500 --> 00:35:57.335
you can get which encrypt all

00:35:57.336 --> 00:35:58.865
the data on it, and to decrypt it

00:35:58.865 --> 00:36:00.382
you have to enter in a PIN code.

00:36:01.109 --> 00:36:02.913
Storing stuff on an encrypted USB stick

00:36:02.915 --> 00:36:05.025
is a pretty good idea, especially since

00:36:05.028 --> 00:36:06.610
things like mobile phones can't decrypt

00:36:06.612 --> 00:36:08.111
a hard drive to interact with it.

00:36:08.356 --> 00:36:09.828
You should treat the internet as

00:36:09.830 --> 00:36:11.243
a hostile place, because it is.

00:36:11.506 --> 00:36:13.683
Be very, very cautious when downloading

00:36:13.687 --> 00:36:15.457
things, clicking links, installing

00:36:15.457 --> 00:36:17.669
stuff, accepting pop-up options.

00:36:18.153 --> 00:36:20.105
For me personally, I try to adopt a

00:36:20.105 --> 00:36:21.946
very minimal approach when it comes

00:36:21.946 --> 00:36:23.685
to the software and apps I use.

00:36:23.981 --> 00:36:25.466
The fewer the better, because

00:36:25.466 --> 00:36:27.134
it reduces the attack surfaces

00:36:27.421 --> 00:36:28.566
for things that can go wrong.

00:36:28.962 --> 00:36:30.698
For Pete’s sake, cover your cameras.

00:36:30.700 --> 00:36:31.857
I think a lot of us are already

00:36:31.857 --> 00:36:32.982
in the habit of covering our

00:36:32.982 --> 00:36:34.662
laptop cameras, which is great.

00:36:35.110 --> 00:36:36.484
But what about your phone camera?

00:36:36.706 --> 00:36:38.351
I’m seeing cases these days that have a

00:36:38.352 --> 00:36:40.393
little slider on the back of the phone

00:36:40.393 --> 00:36:42.072
so it covers the camera, and I love that.

00:36:42.073 --> 00:36:43.104
I have one of those myself.

00:36:43.469 --> 00:36:44.881
But what about the front camera?

00:36:44.984 --> 00:36:47.248
I haven't seen any cases that cover that.

00:36:47.676 --> 00:36:49.128
There are little camera covers that you

00:36:49.129 --> 00:36:50.975
can stick on it, but in my experience,

00:36:50.975 --> 00:36:52.839
they just always pop off after a few days.

00:36:53.338 --> 00:36:54.511
I’ve actually experienced with a

00:36:54.511 --> 00:36:56.149
ton of different types of tape.

00:36:56.501 --> 00:36:57.919
Electrical tape is easy to peel off

00:36:57.930 --> 00:36:59.184
for a photo and it doesn't leave much

00:36:59.185 --> 00:37:01.324
residue, but you need to swap the tape out

00:37:01.325 --> 00:37:02.824
every month or so or else it gets gooey.

00:37:03.189 --> 00:37:04.587
I just don't trust cameras to

00:37:04.592 --> 00:37:06.725
be off when I think they're off

00:37:06.742 --> 00:37:08.154
because of stories like this.

00:37:08.490 --> 00:37:10.639
I also unplug the TV when I go into hotel

00:37:10.640 --> 00:37:12.600
rooms when I stay there, since a lot of

00:37:12.600 --> 00:37:14.042
them have cameras and mics in them, too.

00:37:14.616 --> 00:37:15.774
Of course you should keep

00:37:15.776 --> 00:37:17.607
your system and apps updated.

00:37:17.859 --> 00:37:19.527
Use a different complex password

00:37:19.529 --> 00:37:20.915
for every service app and

00:37:20.935 --> 00:37:22.120
website you have an account for.

00:37:22.370 --> 00:37:23.011
[Music] Actually, I use a

00:37:23.011 --> 00:37:24.285
different e-mail address for

00:37:24.287 --> 00:37:26.027
every account that I have as well.

00:37:26.029 --> 00:37:27.607
This way I immediately know if something

00:37:27.607 --> 00:37:29.448
doesn't look right because it’ll be for an

00:37:29.448 --> 00:37:31.395
e-mail that I only use for one thing, and

00:37:31.435 --> 00:37:32.571
now I’m getting something else from it.

00:37:32.839 --> 00:37:34.519
It’s not a bad idea to use an

00:37:34.528 --> 00:37:35.964
antivirus scan every now and then to

00:37:35.966 --> 00:37:37.589
check for malware on your devices.

00:37:37.976 --> 00:37:39.210
I’m not gonna plug any here, though,

00:37:39.210 --> 00:37:40.420
but do some research and find

00:37:40.420 --> 00:37:42.008
one that’s trusted and reputable.

00:37:42.827 --> 00:37:44.427
I’m not sure we can achieve perfect

00:37:44.429 --> 00:37:46.589
privacy or security, but like I’ve

00:37:46.590 --> 00:37:47.914
said before, when you're trying to

00:37:47.914 --> 00:37:49.406
secure your stuff, it’s kinda like

00:37:49.406 --> 00:37:51.212
running from a bear in the woods.

00:37:51.425 --> 00:37:52.665
You don't need to be faster than

00:37:52.666 --> 00:37:54.156
the bear; you just need to be faster

00:37:54.156 --> 00:37:55.555
than your friend who’s also running

00:37:55.557 --> 00:37:57.321
from the bear in order to stay alive.

00:37:57.539 --> 00:38:00.297
Your goal is to make it hard for an

00:38:00.298 --> 00:38:02.624
attacker to get to your stuff so that

00:38:02.624 --> 00:38:04.586
they just move on to an easier target.

00:38:16.332 --> 00:38:18.199
Outro: [Outro music] This show is created

00:38:18.199 --> 00:38:18.259
by me, Papa Ransom, Jack Rhysider.

00:38:18.640 --> 00:38:19.834
This one was written by

00:38:19.906 --> 00:38:21.686
motherboard, Yale Grauer.

00:38:22.096 --> 00:38:23.901
Our editor is the gigabyter, Tristan

00:38:23.901 --> 00:38:25.864
Ledger, sound design by the LFO,

00:38:25.895 --> 00:38:27.817
Garrett Tiedemann, mixing by Proximity

00:38:27.817 --> 00:38:29.174
Sound, and our intro music is by

00:38:29.178 --> 00:38:30.951
the mysterious Breakmaster Cylinder.

00:38:31.417 --> 00:38:32.279
If you haven't checked it out

00:38:32.279 --> 00:38:33.176
already, you should go listen

00:38:33.176 --> 00:38:35.365
to my other podcast called LOW.

00:38:35.589 --> 00:38:37.893
It’s the craziest story I’ve ever told.

00:38:37.995 --> 00:38:39.136
It’s the craziest story I’ve ever

00:38:39.136 --> 00:38:40.806
heard, and it just might change

00:38:40.806 --> 00:38:42.158
the way you think about life.

00:38:42.792 --> 00:38:45.372
Go find LOW wherever you listen

00:38:45.372 --> 00:38:47.837
to podcasts, spelled L-O-W.

